{
  "title": "Scapulothoracic Crepitus",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3061/scapulothoracic-crepitus",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 22 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Scapulothoracic crepitus, or snapping scapula syndrome, manifests as pain at the scapulothoracic junction with overhead activity.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with painful crepitus of the scapulothoracic joint with forward flexion and improvement of pain with stabilization of the scapula.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is mainly nonoperative with NSAIDs, scapular strenghthening exercises, postural training and activity modifications.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "predisposing abnormal anatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "6% of scapulae have some superomedial hooking",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "malunion of scapula or rib fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "history of resection of 1st rib for thoracic outlet syndrome",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**overuse** with normal anatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inflammation from overuse results in **chronic inflammation**, causing bursal fibrosis, **bursitis**, snapping",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**bony or soft tissue masses**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**osteochondroma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**elastofibroma dorsi**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3061/images/elastofibroma%20ct.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "a benign soft tissue tumor",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "scapular chondrosarcoma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Scoliosis, kyphosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**scapulothoracic dyskinesis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology - Scapula",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "spans ribs 2 to 7",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "three borders (superior, lateral, medial)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**three angles** (superomedial, inferomedial, lateral)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "no direct bony articulation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**no true synovial articulation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Muscles",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**trapezius**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**serratus anterior**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**subscapularis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**levator scapulae**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**rhomboids**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "supraspinatus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "infraspinatus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "teres minor",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "teres major",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "triceps brachii (long head)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "biceps brachii",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "coracobracialis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "deltoid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pectoralis minor",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "latissimus dorsi (small slip of origin)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "omohyoid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ligaments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "transverse scapular ligament - separates suprascapular artery (above) from suprascapular nerve (below, in suprascapular notch)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Blood Supply",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3061/images/nv.jpg",
              "caption": "Relative neurovascular anatomy about the scapula. Gaskill JAAOS 2013."
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "dorsal scapular artery runs deep to rhomboids and levator 1 to 2 cm medial to scapula",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bursae",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3061/images/bursae.jpg",
              "caption": "Right shoulder showing typical bursae about the scapula. Gaskill JAAOS 2013"
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3061/images/bursae_2.jpg",
              "caption": "Axial cross section of scapulothoracic articulation with relevant bursae. Gaskill JAAOS 2013."
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Anatomic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "infraserratus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "supraserratus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Adventitial (pathologic)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**near superior or inferior angles**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inconsistently identified",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "presentation ranges from mild discomfort to significant disability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "trauma and overuse have both been reported",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**patient complains of \"popping\" of scapula**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**painful crepitus** with elevation of arm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain relieved with stabilization of scapula",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fixed or postural kyphosis may be present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**tenderness** or fullness of symptomatic bursa",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**ask patient to demonstrate symptomatic motions**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "passive scapulothoracic motion by examiner may also reproduce crepitus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "scapulothoracic **dyskinesis** may be present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "evaluate for **winging**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "test muscle strength",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "trapezius",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "serratus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "rhomboids",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "levator",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "latissimus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP, lateral and axillary",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "look for osseous abnormalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "osseous lesion on plain radiographs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "soft tissue masses",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inflamed bursae",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Diagnostic injections",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "selective injection of local anesthetic and/or corticosteroid to **point of maximal tenderness** can be diagnostic and therapeutic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Cervical pathology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can be referred to shoulder girdle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDs, scapular strengthening exercises, postural training, activity modification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "no mass or aggressive lesion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "local corticosteroid injections",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "second line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "bursectomy (open or arthroscopic), resection of osseous lesion, resection of scapular border",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "cases refractory to nonoperative treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "improvement in symptoms reported with both open and arthroscopic",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**better results in patients who responded well to injection**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**incomplete resolution of symptoms common** despite improvement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "better results with addition of partial scapulectomy (vs bursectomy alone)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Open",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "position",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "prone, extremity draped free",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "vertical incision over medial border of scapula, centered on symptomatic bursa",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "trapezius split in line with fibers",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "rhomboids and levator elevated subperiosteally",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bursa excised",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "angle of scapula can be excised",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "detached muscles repaired through drill holes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "postoperative care",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "sling immediate post op",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "must protect repaired muscle attachments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "immobilize x 4 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "active motion at 8 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "strengthening at 12 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pros and cons",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pros: wide exposure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cons: morbid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Arthroscopic",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "position",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "prone, extremity draped free, **arm in maximum internal rotation** with hand over lumbar spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "portals: 3 cm medial to medial border of scapula (**avoids dorsal scapular nerve and vessels**) and below scapular spine (**avoids spinal accessory nerve**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
